# Renault 25 phase 1 five-door hatchback, 1984-1988.
#
# The first-generation Renault 25, the firm's executive car, on sale in Britain
# from the beginning of 1984 and facelifted in June 1988; production ended in
# February 1992. The phase-1 car is the shape modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renault_25 (cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.713 x 1.806 x 1.410 m, wheelbase 2.718 m. Source: the reference
# pack's notes, from the Renault 25 dimension box. The hull measures 4.713 m on
# a 2.718 m wheelbase (57.7 per cent) and 1.806 m wide; mirrors take it to
# 1.985 m.
#
# Shape reference: no true side elevation of a phase-1 car exists in the
# Commons categories used. The flank was built from a front-left three-quarter
# of a black car, a near-head-on front-right view of a blue car and a rear-left
# view of the black car, with the wheel centres fixed by the published ratio.
# The defining feature is the fastback hatch that slopes in one continuous line
# from the roof to a high, short tail.
#
# After the first build the side glazing and the number plates were found to be
# nearly flush with the body; a bounded fix moved the side panes 15 mm outward
# and gave the plates a 7.5 mm stand-off. Both side window bands now show in the
# true side elevation.
#
# Colours: no British-market colours were established, so the objects carry
# plain names: silver, blue, grey and red. Weights silver 3, blue 3, grey 2,
# red 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 190 km/h, the 2.0-litre injection car's quoted maximum. Comfort
# 90/465, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 90: a soft-riding executive hatchback, the
# most comfortable Renault of its era. Classes 2,3,4.
#
# Dates are road presence: January 1984 intro, retires staggered 1998-2001 on a
# fourteen- to seventeen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/renault-25-phase1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/renault-25-phase1.dae (91 objects). References:
# citycars/references/renault-25-phase1/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the body is more angular than the photographs and the
# glazing was re-seated after the first pass. At 128 px the long low nose, the
# fastback hatch and the high short tail read as the Renault 25.

obj=citycar
name=Renault25Phase1(Silver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1984
intro_month=1
retire_year=2001
retire_month=6
speed=190
length=3
class=2,3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=90
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=465

Image[E]=./images/renault-25-phase1-silver_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/renault-25-phase1-silver_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/renault-25-phase1-silver_S.0.0,0,0
Image[SW]=./images/renault-25-phase1-silver_SW.0.0,-8,10
Image[W]=./images/renault-25-phase1-silver_W.0.0,4,5
Image[NW]=./images/renault-25-phase1-silver_NW.0.0,12,10
Image[N]=./images/renault-25-phase1-silver_N.0.0,0,33
Image[NE]=./images/renault-25-phase1-silver_NE.0.0,0,24
